From f6e53a3f40159cc089162a651957d5ed3b757efb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 13:08:01 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(sim): verify refuses a non-finite or zero tool axis and
 normalises a scaled one

The NonFinite law checked a move's from/to but not its tool axis: an
axis like [1e-12, 0, inf] read as tilted and the reach law convicted
nothing, and a 7x-scaled axis lost its ShankHit because reach reads
a[2] as a unit component.

verify now passes the path through one door (verify/axis_door.rs)
before any law: a non-finite, zero-length or overflowing axis is
refused by Warning::NonFinite (kept as stated, so each law's own guard
still fires), and a finite axis off unit length by more than 1e-12 in
|a|^2 is normalised once in a copy the laws read. Unit axes pass bit
for bit through a borrowed Cow, so no existing verdict moves.

Pinned by tests/axis_door.rs (both reproductions); radial_rapids'
zero-axis test now also expects the NonFinite refusal.

Fixes #1312

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
